1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,033
You're the one with the problem

2
00:00:01,033 --> 00:00:02,466
You're just afraid Daniel's frogs are better than yours

3
00:00:02,466 --> 00:00:03,100
I know

4
00:00:03,100 --> 00:00:04,533
It's hard to admit you were wrong

5
00:00:04,533 --> 00:00:05,266
But it's fine

6
00:00:05,300 --> 00:00:06,300
When Walter gives the multi-million order

7
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:07,200
to Daniel

8
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:08,000
you'll be on your knees admitting it

9
00:00:08,933 --> 00:00:10,433
Business isn't about who works the hardest

10
00:00:10,700 --> 00:00:11,900
It's about having good judgment

11
00:00:11,900 --> 00:00:12,400
And putting people to good use

12
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:13,466
In this regard

13
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:14,100
you're far behind

14
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:15,533
Words can't save a doomed man

15
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:16,700
Uncle

16
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:17,833
There's something wrong with this bucket of frogs

17
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:18,533
Don't eat them

18
00:00:18,933 --> 00:00:20,033
They look fine to me

19
00:00:27,266 --> 00:00:28,266
Monster

20
00:00:35,633 --> 00:00:36,700
Lewes

21
00:00:36,700 --> 00:00:37,500
The four months are up

22
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:38,166
I'm here for the goods

23
00:00:38,200 --> 00:00:38,933
After you, Mr. Walter

24
00:00:40,333 --> 00:00:41,833
Wait, Mr. Walter

25
00:00:43,066 --> 00:00:43,733
You are

26
00:00:43,833 --> 00:00:45,100
I'm Daniel from the farm across the way

27
00:00:45,333 --> 00:00:46,066
Listen to me

28
00:00:46,400 --> 00:00:47,300
Lewes's frogs have problems

29
00:00:47,600 --> 00:00:48,333
All his workers ran away

30
00:00:48,333 --> 00:00:49,133
The frogs have been starving for days

31
00:00:49,233 --> 00:00:49,966
He can't deliver at all

32
00:00:50,066 --> 00:00:50,766
Exactly

33
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:52,400
All of Lewes's workers ran off

34
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:53,666
I heard the frogs all starved to death

35
00:00:53,666 --> 00:00:54,466
I heard that too

36
00:00:54,533 --> 00:00:55,966
He mistreated his workers and drove them away

37
00:00:56,100 --> 00:00:57,100
No one is working for him

38
00:00:57,100 --> 00:00:57,733
Mr. Walter

39
00:00:57,733 --> 00:00:59,033
I used to work for Lewes

40
00:00:59,066 --> 00:00:59,800
When I left

41
00:00:59,833 --> 00:01:01,033
his frogs were thin and small

42
00:01:01,033 --> 00:01:01,933
They were on the verge of dying

43
00:01:02,300 --> 00:01:02,966
Lewes

44
00:01:03,233 --> 00:01:04,166
Frogs that don't meet the standard

45
00:01:04,200 --> 00:01:04,833
I won't accept

46
00:01:04,833 --> 00:01:05,500
According to the contract

47
00:01:05,700 --> 00:01:07,166
you must pay me a thirty million penalty

48
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:07,633
Walter

49
00:01:07,633 --> 00:01:08,300
My frogs are fine

50
00:01:08,466 --> 00:01:09,466
You'll see if you take a look yourself

51
00:01:09,500 --> 00:01:10,700
Stop wasting Walter's time

52
00:01:11,033 --> 00:01:11,433
Walter

53
00:01:11,700 --> 00:01:12,166
His frogs

54
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:13,133
haven't been cared for in a month

55
00:01:13,433 --> 00:01:14,100
Even if they aren't all dead

56
00:01:14,433 --> 00:01:15,700
they definitely won't meet your standard

57
00:01:15,933 --> 00:01:16,366
How about

58
00:01:16,533 --> 00:01:17,533
you look at my frogs first

59
00:01:17,700 --> 00:01:18,500
Big and fat

60
00:01:18,666 --> 00:01:19,300
And the price

61
00:01:19,400 --> 00:01:20,300
is thirty percent lower than Lewes's

62
00:01:20,466 --> 00:01:21,100
Well

63
00:01:21,233 --> 00:01:22,033
Lewes

64
00:01:22,033 --> 00:01:22,566
Look

65
00:01:22,600 --> 00:01:24,033
Business is about comparing options

66
00:01:24,266 --> 00:01:25,066
I understand

67
00:01:25,266 --> 00:01:26,266
Go check out his place first

68
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:27,233
After you look around

69
00:01:27,266 --> 00:01:28,133
it won't be too late to decide

70
00:01:29,066 --> 00:01:29,666
Let's go

71
00:01:29,833 --> 00:01:30,866
After you
